# ── Files with local overrides (tracked but ignored locally) ──
# NOTE: `app/portfolio/routes.py` used to be listed here. It never had any
# effect — git cannot ignore a tracked file, so `git check-ignore` reported it
# as not ignored — but tools that match these patterns WITHOUT consulting the
# git index (e.g. `railway up` building its upload tarball) dropped the file
# and the image then died on `from app.portfolio import routes`. Use
# `git update-index --skip-worktree <file>` for local-override workflows
# instead of listing a tracked path here.
stratergy.md
